# tools/co/comment_citation_witness.rish -- a path a program cites in a comment still resolves.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. This tree keeps a promise for documents and had never kept it for programs.
# tools/t/tracked_link_witness.rish reads relative links inside `.md` and refuses a broken one; a
# `.rye` module makes the same promise in its doc comments -- `//! Ground: [`spec`](../x.md)` -- and
# nothing read those at all.
#
# So when the `tools/` fold of 20260823.144100 carried 1,917 entries into 35 rooms,
# tools/rye/session_logs_archive.rye moved one directory deeper and its two comment citations kept
# the depth they were written at, pointing at `tools/ORGANIZING.md` and `tools/.claude/`, which have
# never existed. Two repointers ran that day and one link guard stands, and a Markdown link inside a
# `.rye` comment falls between all three. Two more broke when a design note folded into
# `active-designing/yonder/`. Four in all, found on 20260825 by a meter looking at something else.
#
# WHAT IS CHECKED, and gated at ZERO. Every tracked file the card reads as a PROGRAM and that
# carries `](`, read through tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh -- the reading is CITED rather than
# copied, so what counts as a citation is decided in one place. Measured at seating: 85 programs
# scanned, 0 broken. Measured 20260831: 95 programs scanned, 13 prose files skipped, 0 broken. The
# population is small and closed, so a ratchet would be the wrong shape; there is nothing to migrate.
#
# WHAT THE READING ALREADY KNOWS, each learned from a real case rather than imagined:
#
#   a placeholder shape is an illustration    `](date/YYYYMMDD/name)`, `](date/<day>/name)`.
#   a backticked span illustrates syntax      `](./x)` inside backticks in exec_bit_scan.sh.
#   a target must look like a path            `x[1](32000)` is index-then-value arithmetic.
#   link syntax in CODE is emitted data       a row a tool prints into a page two directories away.
#   a symlink's citations belong to its body  pond/apps/granary/wov_core.rye is mode 120000.
#
# The last one is the one that would have done damage. Six symlinked doors read as eleven broken
# citations, and repairing them would have written through the links into six correct bodies and
# broken all six at their real homes. git lists the body alone, so each is read exactly once.
#
# WHOSE POPULATION THIS IS, and why the card is asked rather than answered for (REDS %398). Two of
# those exclusions run only where the card reads a file as a program: it strips backtick spans, and
# it drops a target that does not look like a path, both gated on `truth_source=comments`. A file
# the card reads as PROSE gets neither, and tools/t/tracked_link_witness.rish is its guard. The card
# gained `.bron` and `.kyri` as prose on 20260831 (%392) and this scan's candidate filter kept its
# own older list, so 13 dated session logs arrived here as programs. Read whole, their
# `](../REDS.md)` inside backticks and their bare `](kumara.rye)` produced 10 broken citations
# against a gate of zero, on every body's roster at once -- and all 13 sit in dated testimony, which
# accrete-never-break keeps whole. A guard whose only available repair is forbidden can never go
# green. So the scan asks the card per file and counts what it skips, rather than keeping a second
# list of prose extensions beside the card's own.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal. Twenty behaviors on a real git repository in a throwaway pen -- a broken
# citation bitten, named, and counted; each of the five blessed shapes above left free; a symlinked
# door adding nothing and a body's break reported once against the body rather than a door; prose
# left to its own guard; the card proven load-bearing, since losing it makes the scan refuse rather
# than report zero; a prose notation skipped and that skip COUNTED, since a skip nobody can see
# cannot be told from a guard that stopped reading; the identical broken target inside a program
# still refused, planted and then removed, so the skip turns on the file's class rather than on its
# content; and every extension the speed prefilter drops proven to be one the card independently
# calls prose, which is the case that would have caught this drift on the lap it entered.
#
# WHAT IS NOT CHECKED. Whether the cited document still SAYS what the comment claims. That is
# .claude/rules/docs-implementation-sync.md's job, and only a reader can do it.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Rule: .claude/rules/docs-implementation-sync.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/co/comment_citation_witness.rish

say "comment-citation: Language EN -- a citation is a promise, and a program makes them in its comments."
say "comment-citation: Style Gauge -- one reading, cited from the report card rather than spelled again beside it."
say "comment-citation: Lens TAME -- references are promises; a path that moved is repointed rather than left to a reader to discover."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/comment_citation_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "comment-citation: a program cites a path that does not resolve -- read its own line"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "broken_citations=0" else "comment-citation: this reading is gated at zero, because the population is small and closed"
assert scan.out contains "prose_skipped=" else "comment-citation: what the scan skips is named and counted, never dropped in silence"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "comment-citation: the scan must agree with itself before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- every path a program cites in a comment resolves on this tree"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/comment_citation_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "comment-citation: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "resolving_citation_free=yes" else "comment-citation: a citation that lands must cost nothing"
assert control.out contains "broken_citation_bitten=yes" else "comment-citation: a citation that lands nowhere must refuse -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing"
assert control.out contains "broken_citation_named=yes" else "comment-citation: a broken citation must be named, so it can be repaired"
assert control.out contains "broken_citation_counted=yes" else "comment-citation: and counted, so the reading can be trusted"
assert control.out contains "code_line_free=yes" else "comment-citation: link syntax in code is data the program emits, relative to where that output lands"
assert control.out contains "placeholder_free=yes" else "comment-citation: a placeholder shape illustrates a path rather than citing one"
assert control.out contains "backticked_syntax_free=yes" else "comment-citation: a backticked span illustrates syntax"
assert control.out contains "math_notation_free=yes" else "comment-citation: array-index-then-value arithmetic is not a citation"
assert control.out contains "body_listed_once=yes" else "comment-citation: git lists the body alone, so a body is read once rather than once per door"
assert control.out contains "symlink_door_adds_nothing=yes" else "comment-citation: a second door onto one body must add no reading"
assert control.out contains "body_break_reported_once=yes" else "comment-citation: a body's break is reported once"
assert control.out contains "body_named_not_door=yes" else "comment-citation: and names the body, which is where the repair belongs"
assert control.out contains "prose_left_to_its_own_guard=yes" else "comment-citation: prose has its own link guard; this one reads programs"
assert control.out contains "card_load_bearing=yes" else "comment-citation: the reading is cited, so losing the card must refuse rather than report zero"
assert control.out contains "prose_notation_skipped=yes" else "comment-citation: a file the card calls prose belongs to the link guard, not to this one"
assert control.out contains "prose_skip_counted=yes" else "comment-citation: and the skip is counted, since a skip nobody can see cannot be told from a guard that stopped reading"
assert control.out contains "same_target_in_program_bitten=yes" else "comment-citation: the identical target inside a program must still refuse -- the skip turns on the file's class, never on its content"
assert control.out contains "same_target_named=yes" else "comment-citation: and that refusal names the program, so it can be repaired"
assert control.out contains "same_target_removed_returns_green=yes" else "comment-citation: removing the plant must return the reading to green, so the refusal is shown from both sides"
assert control.out contains "prefilter_matches_card_prose=yes" else "comment-citation: every extension the speed prefilter drops must be one the card independently calls prose, or the two lists drift again"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "comment-citation: the control must agree with itself"
say "twenty behaviors proven on a real git repository, the refusal shown as hard as the welcome"

say "GREEN: comment-citation -- every path a program cites in a comment resolves."
